WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.512
Now compare the second day with the first.

2
00:00:02.512 --> 00:00:05.582
You'll see each kind of
result, and one matters most:

3
00:00:05.582 --> 00:00:08.875
a check whose read failed
with an access-denied error.

4
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:12.837
Its finding isn't resolved; it's
unverified, and stays open.

5
00:00:12.837 --> 00:00:15.978
Draft the issues and search
for a person's name:

6
00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:18.788
it isn't there, only
the object identifier.

7
00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:21.386
Package the second run,
chained to the first,

8
00:00:21.386 --> 00:00:24.850
and verify it with the pipeline
and with the standard tool.

9
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.363
Then tamper with one file,
and verification fails.

10
00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:31.313
Swap the runs, and the comparison refuses.

11
00:00:31.313 --> 00:00:33.940
Run the tests, and seventy-four pass.
